@prefix ldh:    <https://w3id.org/atomgraph/linkeddatahub#> .
@prefix rdf:    <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix dh:     <https://www.w3.org/ns/ldt/document-hierarchy#> .
@prefix dct:    <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

<> a dh:Item ;
    dct:title "Documents" ;
    dct:description "Document structure and the basic data management actions" ;
    rdf:_1 <#content> .

<#content> a ldh:XHTML ;
    rdf:value """<div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
    <p class="lead">Document structure and the basic data management actions</p>
    <div>
        <h2 id="hierarchy">Document hierarchy</h2>
        <p>The basic structure of resources in a LinkedDataHub <a href="../../dataspace/#applications">application</a> is analogous to a file system, but built using RDF
            resources and relationships between them instead. There is a hierarchy of <dfn>containers</dfn> (folders),
            which are collections of <dfn>items</dfn> (files) as well as sub-containers (sub-folders). Both containers
            (instances of <code>dh:Container</code>) and items (instances of <code>dh:Item</code>) are <dfn>documents</dfn> (instances of <code>foaf:Document</code>). Items cannot contain other documents.</p>
        <p>The first level of resources in a container is referred to as its <dfn>children</dfn> (of which that container
            is the <dfn>parent</dfn>), while all levels down the hierarchy are collectively referred to as
            <dfn>descendants</dfn>. In the <a href="https://github.com/AtomGraph/LinkedDataHub-Apps/tree/master/demo/northwind-traders" target="_blank">Northwind Traders</a> dataspace used in the examples below:</p>
        <pre>https://localhost:4443/          # the root container
├── categories/                  # container
│   ├── 1/                       # item — the Beverages category
│   └── …
├── products/                    # container
│   ├── 1/                       # item — the Chai product
│   └── …
└── orders/                      # container</pre>
        <p>When a user logs in, the application loads its root container (unless a specific URI was requested). From there,
            users can navigate down the resource hierarchy, starting with children of the <dfn>root container</dfn>. At
            any moment there is only one <dfn>current document</dfn> per page, on which <a href="#management">management actions</a> can
            be performed: it can be viewed, edited etc.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
        <h2 id="containers">Containers</h2>
        <div>
            <h3 id="container-rdf-serialization">RDF serialization</h3>
            <p>Document properties such as <code>sioc:has_parent</code>, <code>dct:created</code>, <code>dct:modified</code>, <code>acl:owner</code> are <a href="../../http-api/#document-metadata">automatically managed</a> by LinkedDataHub.</p>
            <pre>@prefix dh: &lt;https://www.w3.org/ns/ldt/document-hierarchy#&gt; .
@prefix ldh: &lt;https://w3id.org/atomgraph/linkeddatahub#&gt; .
@prefix rdf: &lt;http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#&gt; .
@prefix dct: &lt;http://purl.org/dc/terms/&gt; .
@prefix xsd: &lt;http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#&gt; .
@prefix sioc: &lt;http://rdfs.org/sioc/ns#&gt; .
@prefix acl: &lt;http://www.w3.org/ns/auth/acl#&gt; .

&lt;https://localhost:4443/categories/&gt;
    a       dh:Container ;
    rdf:_1  &lt;https://localhost:4443/categories/#select-children&gt; ;
    dct:created "2025-06-02T19:12:26.533Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dct:creator &lt;https://admin.localhost:4443/acl/agents/865c2431-8436-4ae8-b300-2a531a013cd0/#this&gt; ;
    dct:title "Categories" ;
    sioc:has_parent &lt;https://localhost:4443/&gt; ;
    acl:owner &lt;https://admin.localhost:4443/acl/agents/865c2431-8436-4ae8-b300-2a531a013cd0/#this&gt; .

&lt;https://localhost:4443/categories/#select-children&gt;
    a       ldh:Object ;
    rdf:value ldh:ChildrenView .</pre>
            <p>The <code>&lt;#select-children&gt;</code> resource is an <code>ldh:Object</code> <a href="../blocks/">content block</a> whose <code>rdf:value</code> <code>ldh:ChildrenView</code> renders the container's children listing.</p>
            <p class="exhibit-links">Live: <a href="https://northwind-traders.demo.linkeddatahub.com/categories/" target="_blank">/categories/</a> (the demo's version composes <a href="https://github.com/AtomGraph/LinkedDataHub-Apps/blob/master/demo/northwind-traders/categories.ttl" target="_blank">further blocks</a> on top of this shape)</p>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div>
        <h2 id="items">Items</h2>
        <div>
            <h3 id="item-rdf-serialization">RDF serialization</h3>
            <p>Document properties such as <code>sioc:has_container</code>, <code>dct:created</code>, <code>dct:modified</code>, <code>acl:owner</code> are <a href="../../http-api/#document-metadata">automatically managed</a> by LinkedDataHub.</p>
            <pre>@prefix dh: &lt;https://www.w3.org/ns/ldt/document-hierarchy#&gt; .
@prefix dct: &lt;http://purl.org/dc/terms/&gt; .
@prefix xsd: &lt;http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#&gt; .
@prefix sioc: &lt;http://rdfs.org/sioc/ns#&gt; .
@prefix acl: &lt;http://www.w3.org/ns/auth/acl#&gt; .
@prefix foaf: &lt;http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/&gt; .
@prefix schema: &lt;https://schema.org/&gt; .

&lt;https://localhost:4443/products/1/&gt;
    a       dh:Item ;
    dct:created "2025-06-02T19:49:48.126Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dct:creator &lt;https://admin.localhost:4443/acl/agents/865c2431-8436-4ae8-b300-2a531a013cd0/#this&gt; ;
    dct:title "Chai" ;
    sioc:has_container &lt;https://localhost:4443/products/&gt; ;
    acl:owner &lt;https://admin.localhost:4443/acl/agents/865c2431-8436-4ae8-b300-2a531a013cd0/#this&gt; ;
    foaf:primaryTopic &lt;https://localhost:4443/products/1/#this&gt; .

&lt;https://localhost:4443/products/1/#this&gt;
    a       schema:Product ;
    schema:name "Chai" ;
    schema:identifier "1" ;
    schema:category &lt;https://localhost:4443/categories/1/#this&gt; ;
    schema:provider &lt;https://localhost:4443/suppliers/1/#this&gt; .</pre>
            <p>An item is often <em>about</em> something — here the document <samp>products/1/</samp> describes the Chai product, a non-information
                resource identified by the <samp>#this</samp> fragment and linked with <code>foaf:primaryTopic</code>.</p>
            <p class="exhibit-links">Source: <a href="https://github.com/AtomGraph/LinkedDataHub-Apps/blob/master/demo/northwind-traders/products/products.rq" target="_blank">products/products.rq</a> (the mapping that mints it) · Live: <a href="https://northwind-traders.demo.linkeddatahub.com/products/1/" target="_blank">/products/1/</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div>
        <h2 id="management">Management</h2>
        <div class="ldhc-tabs or-horizontal">
            <div class="ldhc-tablist sz-md va-line" role="tablist">
                <button aria-controls="user-interface-pane" aria-selected="true" class="ldhc-tab is-on" id="user-interface-tab" role="tab" type="button"><span class="ldhc-tab-lbl">User interface</span></button>
                <button aria-controls="command-line-interface-pane" aria-selected="false" class="ldhc-tab" id="command-line-interface-tab" role="tab" type="button"><span class="ldhc-tab-lbl">Command line interface</span></button>
            </div>
            <div aria-labelledby="user-interface-tab" class="ldhc-tabpanel" id="user-interface-pane" role="tabpanel">
            <table class="table table-striped">
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th>Action</th>
                        <th>Description</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr>
                        <th>Create</th>
                        <td>Create a new child document by clicking the <span class="btn btn-primary create-action">Create</span> button. Fill out the form. Click <span class="btn btn-primary btn-save">Save</span>.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <th>Update</th>
                        <td>Open the current document editing form by clicking the <span class="btn btn-edit"></span> button in the <a href="../../user-interface/#action-bar">action bar</a>. Make changes. Click <span class="btn btn-primary btn-save">Save</span>.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <th>Delete</th>
                        <td>Delete the current document by clicking the <span class="btn btn-delete"></span> button in the <a href="../../user-interface/#action-bar">action bar</a>.</td>
                    </tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
            </div>
            <div aria-labelledby="command-line-interface-tab" class="ldhc-tabpanel" hidden="hidden" id="command-line-interface-pane" role="tabpanel">
            <table class="table table-striped">
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th>Action</th>
                        <th>CLI command</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr>
                        <th>Create container</th>
                        <td><a href="../../command-line-interface/#commands"><samp>ldh create-container</samp></a></td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <th>Create item</th>
                        <td><a href="../../command-line-interface/#commands"><samp>ldh create-item</samp></a></td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <th>Update</th>
                        <td><a href="../../command-line-interface/#commands"><samp>ldh put</samp></a></td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <th>Delete</th>
                        <td><a href="../../command-line-interface/#commands"><samp>ldh delete</samp></a></td>
                    </tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
            <p>For example, creating the <samp>categories/</samp> container (with the <a href="../../command-line-interface/#environment-variables"><samp>LDH_*</samp> environment variables</a> supplying the certificate and base URI):</p>
            <pre>ldh create-container \\
  --parent "$LDH_BASE" \\
  --title "Categories" \\
  --slug categories</pre>
            <p>The command prints the created document's URL — <samp>https://localhost:4443/categories/</samp>.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <p class="lead">To create documents step-by-step, follow the <a href="../../../user-guide/create-data/create-documents/">Create documents</a> guide</p>
</div>"""^^rdf:XMLLiteral .
